{
  "id": "thermoesthesia",
  "term": "thermoesthesia",
  "definition": "Thermoesthesia is the capacity to sense changes in temperature at the skin, including tactile-like feelings triggered by rapid thermal shifts. In the described illusion, quick warming can feel like upward pressure or motion, whereas quick cooling can feel like a downward or pulling sensation.",
